{%- comment -%}
  Toolbar gender quick-filter buttons - moved out of
  sections/5dla_collection-product-grid.liquid's hardcoded `.c5dla-toolbar
  .genders` (previously static "All genders"/"Men"/"Women"/"Unisex" text,
  none of it wired to anything).

  Looks for the Shopify "target-gender" taxonomy filter among
  `results.filters` (`filter.param_name contains 'target-gender'` - same
  filter snippets/5dla_filter-sort-drawer.liquid renders as an ordinary
  checkbox list/pill group) and renders one button per `filter.values`
  entry, plus a permanent "All genders" button first. Renders nothing if
  this collection has no gender filter at all (e.g. no products carry the
  Shopify gender taxonomy metafield).

  These are a QUICK-FILTER shortcut for that SAME checkbox, not a second,
  parallel filtering mechanism: client/ver_2_0/js/modules/filter-sort.js
  delegates their clicks into a `filter:filterByGender` event, whose
  listener (same file) finds the matching `label[title="..."] input[name=
  "filter.v.t.shopify.target-gender"]` and fires a real `change` on it -
  going through the exact same form "change" → AJAX path every other
  filter field already uses (see that file's own top comment), including
  `applyFilters` re-rendering these buttons' own `active` state afterward
  (`.c5dla-toolbar .genders` is swapped in from the response, same as this
  form's own body/foot).

  Unlike a checkbox, these buttons are one-way: clicking "Men" always
  turns gender filtering ON for Men (never off by clicking it again) -
  "All genders" is the only button that clears it, a single-select
  radio/tab affordance rather than a toggle (see filter-sort.js's
  `filter:filterByGender` listener - it unchecks every gender input first,
  then (re)checks only the clicked one, if any).

  `results` (required): same collection object passed to
  snippets/5dla_filter-sort-drawer.liquid.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign gender_filter = nil
  for filter in results.filters
    if filter.param_name contains 'target-gender'
      assign gender_filter = filter
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- if gender_filter -%}
  <div class="genders">
    <button
      type="button"
      class="{% if gender_filter.active_values.size == 0 %}active{% endif %}"
      data-c5dla-gender-button
      data-gender-title=""
    >
      {{ 'products.facets.all' | t }} genders
    </button>
    {%- for value in gender_filter.values -%}
      <button
        type="button"
        class="{% if value.active %}active{% endif %}"
        data-c5dla-gender-button
        data-gender-title="{{ value.label | escape }}"
      >
        {{ value.label | escape }}
      </button>
    {%- endfor -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
